    "result_text": "Build passes, the test is green. Here's what I changed and why.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe household is now keyed on **(lastName, postcode)** via a deterministic id, and everything that keys off the household uses it.\n\n**`HouseholdId.of(lastName, postcode)`** \u2014 now takes the postcode (was address) and returns the **first 12 hex chars of SHA-256** over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (dropped the old `H-` prefix). This is the single source of truth for the household key.\n\n**Callers updated to feed it postcode and compare via the computed id:**\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the `householdId` DTO mapping now passes `owner.getPostcode()`.\n- `RejectDuplicateHousehold` (the 409 block) \u2014 compares `HouseholdId.of(...)` instead of raw lastName+address strings; still bypasses when `sharesHousehold` is true. So a second owner with the same lastName+postcode is a 409 household duplicate unless it declares membership.\n- `DetectPossibleDuplicate` (the soft flag) \u2014 now matches on the computed householdId, and **exits early without flagging when `sharesHousehold` is true** (reads the request DTO via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`), so a declared member is never a suspected duplicate.\n- `HouseholdTier.isGold` (household-size \u2192 membership tier) \u2014 counts members sharing the postcode-based householdId.\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n- Each edited method stays tiny and single-purpose; I removed the now-redundant local `key()` helper from `RejectDuplicateHousehold` and reused the shared `HouseholdId` rather than duplicating normalization logic.\n- I left the `DuplicateHouseholdException` constructor signature untouched (just passing postcode as the second arg) and skipped touching the large `openapi.yml` doc file, since neither affects behavior \u2014 avoiding extra files in the change set.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: `HouseholdTier` and `MembershipTier` are not currently wired into the live `membershipLevel` mapping (that uses `namesakeCount`). I updated `HouseholdTier` for spec consistency (\"everything that keys off the household\"), but it isn't exercised by any endpoint or test today.",
